cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Does a probe qubit's information backflow diagnose many-body quantum chaos? An exact study on mixed-field Ising environments"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chenchupradeep
    given-names: Degala
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pradeepdegalaroyal/probe-qubit-backflow-vs-chaos-ising-environment"
abstract: >-
  Exact simulation study of a pure-dephasing probe qubit coupled to a 6-12 spin
  mixed-field Ising chain. It tests whether Breuer-Laine-Piilo information backflow
  tracks the integrable-to-chaotic crossover, and compares it with the late-time
  coherence plateau, an out-of-time-order correlator and level-spacing statistics
  under shot noise and extra probe dephasing.
keywords:
  - quantum chaos
  - open quantum systems
  - non-Markovianity
  - Loschmidt echo
  - out-of-time-order correlator
